Well, I say spellcaster, I had to take off the gloves and shield.

Anyway, I  normally play Wiz, but after a disasterous set of games
recently (I think I got to Sokoban only once in 30 games), I decided to
do something a little different.  And so, the Valkyrie it was.

Started off fairly respectably, cat died on level 2 alas, but found a
shine on level 4,  Some heavy lifting, and I sifted through all the
dropped armours, managed to find +2 elven cloak and +2 elven helm by
the mines.  Add in some mithrill, and a decent AC for the low levels.
Ran down to Minetown, then back to the main dungeon, got Excalibur,
burned through the scrolls of create monster by the shirine for
Mjollner.  Down to Sokoban, bag of holding, then back up and clear out
the mines for the luckstone.  So far, so good.

Found a blessed spell book of detect treasue, which, while not of that
much interest, made me wonder.  A quick blessing later, and I knew
magic missile and identify.  Had to loose the shield to cast, but for
ID that's not an issue.

Back down the main dungeon, and ran into a graveyard on level 16,
largest I've ever seen, 3/4 filled with Wraiths.  Carefully cleared the
non wraiths out, grabbed Excalibur, and trew gold to wake them, boogie
on the stairs, and presto, level 21.

A couple of levels later, an opulant throne gave two wishes, which went
on gray dragon scale mail and a shiny, shiny shield of reflection
(already found the gauntlets of power).

After that, it was fairly mechanical - quest nemisis was a walk over,
and half damage, thank you very much.  Genocide went on L, and I was
all set.

Wand of wishing at the castle went on charging scroll, ring of teleport
control (bad accident with a nymph corpse), and a helm of brilliance.
Another went later on a magic marker, with all those blanked scrolls to
enchant things.

Only found one wand of ploymorph, and was polypiling on the back porch
right next to the castle, when I made the dumbest mistake, and straight
in the drink!  Took me ages to realise I'd lost the Orb of Fate in
there, and so the last wish went on an amulet of magical breathing to
get it back!  (Annoyingly, I'j just polypiled the one I'd found, and
all the strangulation/change amulets into liesaving when realised.
Wasted a wish there).

A few more levels gained from potions, and succubi, and into Ghennom.
Cleared the place down, found the square, and then ported up to fix
mind flayer map lossage.  Got crowned, and Ogresmasher (yay, what a
useful weapon...).  Detour to minetown, and at this point I had a net
-50 AC in my gear, with Excalibur and Mjollner fully enchanted.

For normal levels, I'd remove the gauntlets and shield, use spells for
range untill I ran out of power, and then gauntlets on and throwing
hammers.  Repeat.  Once I got to the wizard tower, the shield stayed
on, but then the biggest spell was identify, no longer needed, and cone
of cold, which can be cast with a shield ... sometimes.

I had 7 amulets of lifesaving, -50 AC, two +7 artifcats, 330 hp, 72
power and level 30 by the time I took out Rodney.  Interestingly, he
jumped me like 6 times on the way down (4 levels), and only 5 times
after I had the amulet (58 levels).  One scary moment where he stole
it, and then disappeared off the map - he'd gone down a level, but he'd
done it from the up stairwell ...

Having the gear, the elemental planes were a doddle - the Orb of fate's
4 charges fit nicely with portal finding.  The Astral plane was slow...
died once to Pesilances sickness (forgot I had it, and thus didn't horn
- it's off the edge of the tty window).  Had to tour all three alters -
thank goodness for the summon insects spell.  If there hadn't had been
a few of them around, basically acting as buffers, I might have been
swamped.  As it was, a killer bee was as good as a rest.

72000 turns, 4549710 points.  13 years since I first steered that
little @ around, it's been a while coming.

Nice one, Dev Team.



